Package: globalhex
Title: H3-Style Access to Hierarchical DGGRID Grids
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nicolas", "Gauthier", email = "nicolas.gauthier@ufl.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Kevin", "Sahr", role = c("ctb", "cph"), comment = "Author of the bundled DGGRID source"),
    person("Gerald", "Evenden", role = "cph", comment = "Bundled proj4lib code"),
    person("Frank", "Warmerdam", role = "cph", comment = "Bundled shapelib code"),
    person("Even", "Rouault", role = "cph", comment = "Bundled shapelib code")
    )
Description: An experimental package exposing a small, H3-shaped R API over
    modern DGGRID hierarchical indexes, using a bundled copy of DGGRID. The
    default grid is the equal-area IGEO7 grid with Z7 digit-string indexes.
    ISEA3H with Z3 indexes and a partial compatibility path through dggridR
    are also supported. Large cell datasets can be aggregated through the
    hierarchy and plotted with viewport-aware level of detail before polygon
    geometry is constructed, with automatic raster rendering for large display
    layers. Optional raster helpers provide exact area-weighted extraction and
    fast cell-center sampling from modern terra rasters.
